  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **That's Heaven To Me**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Kentucky Waltz**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **Wonderful (the Way I Feel)**: back after 27 archived shows (631 days) [2]\n- **The Right Place**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 8 archived performances [2]\n- **Look At You**: rare: 13 archived performances [2]\n- **His Master's Voice**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 6 archived performances [2]\n- **Peace In The Valley**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2009-12-06** (recommended): source not stated; 12 songs; 56 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The concert was a benefit for Kentuckians For The Commonwealth [1]\n- Daniel Martin Moore played the opening set, and Jim joined him as a guest for the first two tracks [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2009-12-06**: taped by Brian Porter; source: DPA 4021 (FOB) > Oade m148 > Sony D50 (24/96) [1]",
